Subject: [PATCH 0/2] STM32F469 support: endpoint re-enablement + RAL warning
 hygiene

The STM32F469 OTG core (core_id 0x0000_1200) requires F446-like
endpoint re-enablement after OUT transactions; without it, a
STM32F469I-DISCO device answers EP0 and then goes silent after the
first OUT transaction — no interface endpoint ever delivers data.

Patch 1 adds the core_id to the existing re-enablement condition
(3 functional lines). Patch 2 is independent build hygiene: crate-level
allows for the warnings emitted by the generated RAL code, so
downstream -D warnings builds stay clean; it can be dropped if the
generator should be fixed instead.

Base: f5ed464 ("Merge pull request #55 from stm32-rs/release"), the
v0.5.0 tag and current master tip.

Downstream lifecycle tracked as Amperstrand/ccid-firmware-rs#271; the
fork pin rides Amperstrand/synopsys-usb-otg@764bc042 until an upstream
release carries this.

Amperstrand (2):
  Re-enable endpoints on STM32F469 after OUT transactions
  Suppress warnings from generated RAL code

